<title>USA: Movado Q3 Oct 31 shr rises to $1.22.</title>
<headline>Movado Q3 Oct 31 shr rises to $1.22.</headline>
<dateline>LYNDHURST, N.J. 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>MOVADO GROUP, INC.</p>
<p>		     (in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>					Three months	 Nine months</p>
<p>					1996    1995	1996     1995</p>
<p> Net sales		     $76,864 $68,079  $158,629 $140,269</p>
<p> Cost of sales		  33,897  31,947    70,681   65,909</p>
<p> Gross profit		   42,968  36,132    87,948   74,360</p>
<p>Selling, general &amp;</p>
<p>  administrative expenses   31,439  25,468    72,568   60,863</p>
<p> Operating profit	     11,528  10,664    15,380   13,497</p>
<p> Net interest expense	  1,367   1,369     3,490    3,650</p>
<p> Income before taxes	  10,161   9,295    11,890    9,847</p>
<p> Provision for income taxes  2,811   2,789     3,330    2,954</p>
<p> Net income		     7,350   6,506     8,560  6,893(a)</p>
<p> Net income per share:	  1.22    1.08	1.42  1.15(b)</p>
<p> Avg shares			6,011   6,003     6,009    5,998</p>
<p>NOTE: First nine months 1995 includes one time $600,000 charge or $0.07 per share for adopting new accounting standard.</p>
<p>Full company name is Movado Group Inc.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
